<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Hand-constructed, synthetic TRIAS StopEventResponse fixture - not a
  captured real response. Same provenance/construction approach as
  trias-stop-event-response.xml (see TriasDepartureProviderTest's class
  javadoc and that fixture's own header comment): built by hand from the
  official Trias_StopEvents.xsd / Trias_JourneySupport.xsd /
  Trias_LocationSupport.xsd / Trias_Common.xsd / Trias_ModesSupport.xsd
  schema files.

  Regression fixture for a real bug seen against live KVV (Karlsruhe) data:
  unlike trams (which spell out "Gleis"), KVV's real PlannedBay/EstimatedBay
  text for a BUS departure uses the German abbreviation "Bstg." ("Bussteig" -
  "bus platform/bay"). Two StopEventResult entries, both on-time with
  real-time confirmation, mixing two "Bstg." spelling variants the same way
  the "Gleis" fixture mixes its variants:
    1. mixed case, with the period: "Bstg. 3" / "BSTG. 3"
    2. lowercase, no period, with and without a space: "bstg 21" / "bstg21"

  TriasDepartureProvider.normalizePlatform() must recognize "Bstg." as a
  distinct label from "Gleis" and reformat it into "Bstg. N" - never "Gl.
  Bstg. N" (doubled AND mislabelled as a tram track) or "Gl. N" (mislabelled
  only).
-->
